// ============================================================
// MicroManager Acquisition Script
// ============================================================
// Revision history:
//   2026-05 VK  - Added ConfigureLogging() with async stdout/stderr threads
//   2026-06     - Bug fixes: readTextInfo(), waitForSerial(), setFilename(),
//                 string comparisons, guisavepath fallback
//               - Multi-Pattern redesign: labeled sequence format, 
//                 delay/valve non-capturing steps, derived index parsing
//               - Abort mechanism: volatile flag + confirm dialog
//               - Hardcoded paths consolidated to CONFIG BLOCK below
//
// ============================================================
// SETTINGS FILE FORMAT (Multi-Pattern example):
//
//   Multi-Pattern          <- [0]  experiment type
//   100.0                  <- [1]  exposure (ms)
//   2x2                    <- [2]  binning
//   10.0                   <- [3]  trigger period (ms)
//   5.0                    <- [4]  trigger delay (ms)
//   0                      <- [5]  acquisition speed
//   1                      <- [6]  number of trials / repeats
//   300                    <- [7]  trial duration (frames)
//   60                     <- [8]  trial interval (s)
//   D:\Data\Experiment     <- [9]  save path
//   1a1b2                  <- [10] sequence string (digits=capture, letters=action)
//   1) A50,a150 | P1,2,500,100 % Baseline: air puff + weak stim
//   2) i200,L50,l150 | P1,2,500,200 % Test: strong stim
//   a) delay:5min % Short inter-block pause
//   b) delay:10min % Long inter-block pause
//   c) v3on % Switch valve 3 on before next block
//
// Pattern line format:
//   label) <mc_command> | <stimjim_command> % <comment>
//   - mc_command    : serial string sent to microcontroller (vport)
//   - stimjim_command: optional, sent to StimJim (sport); omit the | if not needed
//   - comment       : optional human-readable note after %; stripped before parsing
//   - For letter-labeled (non-capturing) lines:
//       delay:Xmin or delay:Xs   -> countdown wait, acqCounter not incremented
//       v3on, v2off, etc.        -> sent directly to vport, no image capture
//
// ============================================================

